# Unit tests for bacapp.c (run: make && python3 run_vectors.py tests.vec)
#
# Expected encodings are derived by hand from ASHRAE 135 clause 20.2, not
# captured from the implementation.  Long outputs (> 64 bytes) use the
# driver's "<first 16 bytes>..<fnv1a64>/<len>" form; those expected lines were
# computed with an independent Python model of the byte string.
#
# Every "ERR" below also asserts that the encoder left the buffer untouched
# (the driver would print "ERR DIRTY" otherwise) and every "OK" asserts that
# nothing was written past the capacity (the driver would append "OVERRUN").
#
# Design decisions pinned here (see header comment in bacapp.c):
#   * encoders reject out-of-domain arguments (-1, buffer untouched)
#   * decoders accept only canonical encodings (minimal lengths/integers)
#   * dec_tag decodes the header only; it does not require the content octets

# ---- NULL / BOOLEAN
### null-enc enc
enc_null
---
OK 00

### bool-enc enc
enc_bool 0
enc_bool 1
---
OK 10
OK 11

### null-bool-dec dec
dec_app 00
dec_app 10
dec_app 11
---
OK n=1 null
OK n=1 bool 0
OK n=1 bool 1

### bool-dec-invalid-lvt dec invalid
dec_app 12
dec_app 14
dec_app 150501
---
ERR
ERR
ERR

### null-dec-with-content dec invalid
dec_app 0100
---
ERR

